      "heading": "Refund Windows: The Clock Starts Ticking Immediately",
      "headingZh": "退款窗口：时钟立即开始计时",
      "text": "The refund window is the single most important difference between the two stores, and it is also the most commonly misunderstood. On the Apple App Store, there is no publicly stated fixed refund window. Apple's policy, as described in its terms of service, is that refunds are considered on a case-by-case basis. In practice, the effective window is approximately 30 days for most purchase types, though some categories — such as subscriptions — may be considered for up to 90 days in certain regions. The key point is that Apple's system evaluates each request individually, and the approval rate declines sharply after 14 days. On Google Play, the refund policy is more explicit and more generous in some cases. For apps and games, Google Play offers a two-hour automatic refund window. If you uninstall an app within two hours of purchase, the refund is automatic and requires no human review. After two hours and up to 48 hours, you can still request a refund through the Google Play website, but it goes through a review process. For in-app purchases, Google Play offers a 48-hour refund window for most purchases, though this is not guaranteed. For subscriptions, Google Play allows you to request a refund within 48 hours of the charge, and the process is similar to the App Store — you submit a request and wait for review. The practical difference: Google Play's two-hour automatic refund for apps is the most consumer-friendly policy in the industry, but it applies only to app purchases, not in-app purchases or subscriptions. Apple has no equivalent automatic window. For everything else — in-app purchases, subscriptions, and purchases beyond the two-hour window — the two stores are roughly comparable, with Google Play being slightly more transparent about its review criteria.",
      "textZh": "退款窗口是两个商店之间最重要的区别，也是最常被误解的。在 Apple App Store，没有公开声明的固定退款窗口。Apple 的政策，如其服务条款所述，是退款按个案考虑。实际上，大多数购买类型的有效窗口约为 30 天，尽管某些类别如订阅在某些地区可能被考虑长达 90 天。关键点是 Apple 的系统单独评估每个请求，批准率在 14 天后急剧下降。在 Google Play，退款政策更为明确，在某些情况下更慷慨。对于应用和游戏，Google Play 提供两小时自动退款窗口。如果你在购买后两小时内卸载应用，退款自动进行，无需人工审核。两小时后至 48 小时内，你仍可通过 Google Play 网站请求退款，但需经过审核流程。对于应用内购买，Google Play 为大多数购买提供 48 小时退款窗口，尽管这不保证。对于订阅，Google Play 允许你在扣费后 48 小时内请求退款，流程与 App Store 类似——你提交请求并等待审核。实际区别：Google Play 的两小时自动退款应用是行业中最有利于消费者的政策，但它仅适用于应用购买，而非应用内购买或订阅。Apple 没有同等的自动窗口。对于其他所有——应用内购买、订阅和超过两小时窗口的购买——两个商店大致相当，Google Play 对其审核标准的透明度略高。"
